### Surface deliverable (feature-views/KioskOverlay/)
KioskOverlay.Model.cs / .ViewModel.cs / .cs + Tests/FeatureViews/KioskOverlayTests.cs (36 test cases). Parity
port of web features/dashboard/components/KioskOverlay.tsx: the screen-filling, mostly click-through kiosk
chrome. Every conditional layer of the web source is reproduced and unit-tested:
  - Dim burn-in layer (web isDimmed): a black rectangle at opacity = 1 - dimLevel (clamped 0..1), hit-test
    invisible, exactly as the web inline style.
  - Cursor auto-hide (web isCursorHidden): driven through an idempotent IKioskCursorController; the production
    controller toggles the Win32 cursor display count (user32!ShowCursor via [LibraryImport]) — the canonical
    kiosk technique — only on a real transition so the global counter stays balanced, and restores the cursor
    on Dispose. The controller's transition logic is injected (Action<bool>) so it is unit-tested headlessly
    without touching Win32.
  - Clock overlay (web config.showClock + clockPosition): time (web formatTime, "02:30 PM") over weekday+date
    (web formatDateWithDay, "Mon, Jun 8") anchored to the configured corner, re-projected every second by a
    DispatcherQueueTimer (web setInterval 1000) and exposed to Narrator.
  - Rotation dots (web dashboardCount>1 && config.rotateInterval>0): one dot per dashboard, the active one
    wider, hit-test invisible, decorative to Narrator.
  - Exit affordance (web onExit): a Subtle TsButton (X glyph + "Exit Kiosk"), top-right, always in the tree and
    Narrator-reachable, fading in on pointer activity and hiding after 3s (web mousemove/touchstart -> 3000ms);
    activation raises the ExitRequested event. The fade is an instant opacity change (no storyboard) so the
    system reduced-motion preference is honoured by construction; font sizes scale with the system text-scale.
The web component performs no data fetch (it binds only useTranslation + useDateFormat), so — like the
committed ReferenceLinksSection precedent — there is no loading/error/offline/stale DATA state to fabricate;
the honest native surface reproduces exactly the conditional overlay layers above. All state flows through the
shared KioskOverlayViewModel; the view performs no HTTP. view.opened slug=KioskOverlay is emitted once on open
(PII-safe — no config/time/dashboard value in diagnostics).

### i18n (P1/S10) — every source key resolves in the catalog
The web source passes three keys to t(); all resolve in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw and the shared
catalog (apps/shared/i18n/catalog), so no catalog edit was needed:
  translation.kiosk.exit ("Exit kiosk mode"), translation.kiosk.exitLabel ("Exit Kiosk"),
  translation.dashboard.kiosk ("Kiosk", reused as the accessibility landmark name).
Keys are fully namespaced (translation.*) so they resolve through the shell ResourceLoader bridge in every
shipped language, with the English fallback kept for the headless / missing-resource path.

